<title>BELGIUM: BELGIAN POET HERMAN DE CONINCK DIES IN LISBON.</title>
<headline>BELGIAN POET HERMAN DE CONINCK DIES IN LISBON.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1997-05-22</dateline>
<text>
<p>Belgian poet Herman De Coninck, 52, has died of a heart attack at a literary conference in Lisbon, Portugal, national news agency Belga said on Thursday.</p>
<p>De Coninck, a leading Dutch-language poet, published several collections of poetry, including his popular 1969 debut &quot;De lenige liefde&quot; (Lithe love).</p>
<p>He was also editor of the literary magazine &quot;Nieuw Wereldtijdschrift&quot; and had a literary column in Flemish daily De Morgen.</p>
<p>He was married to Flemish fiction writer Kristien Hemmerechts.</p>
<p>-- Brussels Newsroom +32 2 287 6810, Fax +32 2 230 7710</p>
